spec-rc3-2-message-templates-send-helpers.md:158: "The token-redaction registry (`middleware.redact_token_route`) covers `/reference/*` server-side; the helpers must not add a second leak path." — but middleware.gleam:330 reads: `fn redact_token_route(segments: List(String)) -> Result(String, Nil) {
  case segments {
    ["dsar", ..] -> Ok("/dsar/<redacted>")
    ["erase", ..] -> Ok("/erase/<redacted>")
    // F3 draft capability URLs — the vacancy short_code is not secret (it
    // rides every invite email), the token is.
    ["apply", code, "resume", ..] ->
      Ok("/apply/" <> code <> "/resume/<redacted>")
    ["apply", code, "draft-erasure", ..] ->
      Ok("/apply/" <> code <> "/draft-erasure/<redacted>")
    _ -> Error(Nil)
  }
}` — no ["reference", ..] arm (grep confirms no "reference" anywhere in middleware.gleam/router.gleam).
